+# GAYZE — Communications layer
+
+Deliverable A–O for the reliability brief. Every claim below was verified
+against the code in this repository; anything that could not be verified in this
+environment is labelled as such rather than assumed.
+
+> **Status: migrations authored, NOT applied.** This environment has no database
+> access (no `psql`, no Supabase CLI, no network route to the project). The SQL
+> in `supabase/migrations/` is complete and reviewed but has never been executed
+> against a live database, so RLS behaviour, Realtime payloads and the RPC
+> signatures are reasoned about rather than observed. Apply them in a staging
+> project and run the verification checklist in §O before shipping.
+
+---
+
+## A. Architecture audit
+
+### What the layer did before
+
+```
+App.tsx
+ ├─ subscribeToConversationMessages(activeRoomId)     ← one channel, for the open room only
+ │    └─ postgres_changes INSERT, filtered by conversation_id
+ ├─ webrtcCallService.initUserSignaling(userId)
+ │    └─ Realtime BROADCAST on gayze-user-{userId}
+ └─ webrtcCallService (per call)
+      └─ Realtime BROADCAST on gayze-call-{conversationId}
+           subscribe → send → removeChannel   ← throwaway channel per signal
+```
+
+No service worker, no manifest, no Push API usage, no `notifications` or
+`push_subscriptions` tables, no unread model, and `unreadCount={0}` hardcoded in
+the navigation.
+
+### What it is now
+
+```
+                    ┌───────────────────────────────────────────┐
+  browser           │  realtimeManager                          │
+  ──────────────────┤   ref-counted channels by topic           │
+                    │   backoff reconnect · offline parking      │
+                    │   re-subscribe on visibility regain       │
+                    └───────────────────────────────────────────┘
+                                    │
+   ┌──────────────────┬─────────────┴──────────────┬────────────────────┐
+   │                  │                            │                    │
+gayze-inbox-{user}  gayze-calls-inbox-{user}   gayze-call-signals-{id}  gayze-albums-{user}
+   │                  │                            │                    │
+messages INSERT/    calls INSERT/UPDATE       call_signals INSERT     albums, album_items
+UPDATE/DELETE       (RLS-scoped to the        (per-call, RLS)         (RLS-scoped)
+   │                 member)
+   ▼                  ▼                            ▼
+App inbox handler   incoming call sheet      drain → applySignal → RTCPeerConnection
+   │                                               │
+   ├─ decrypt with the conversation key            ├─ CONNECTED only from connectionState
+   ├─ append (id is the duplicate guard)           ├─ reconnecting grace period
+   ├─ unread++ unless the room is on screen        ├─ ICE restart with renegotiation
+   └─ decideNotification()                         └─ heartbeat → server sweep → MISSED/ENDED
+        │
+        ├─ foreground  → in-app toast (tappable → openConversation)
+        └─ background  → service worker → system notification → deep link
+```
+
+### Realtime mechanism, per concern
+
+| Concern | Mechanism | Why |
+|---|---|---|
+| New/updated/removed messages | `postgres_changes` on `messages`, **unfiltered**, RLS-scoped | One channel for every conversation. RLS means the server decides what a member may receive, so the client does not have to enumerate rooms. |
+| Unread counts | `conversation_unread_counts()` RPC + `conversation_reads` watermark | A watermark is idempotent and self-healing; a counter drifts on a missed event. |
+| Call invitation | `postgres_changes` INSERT on `calls` | A persisted row survives a socket outage. Broadcast is discarded if the callee is not joined — which is the normal state on iOS after backgrounding. |
+| SDP and ICE | `call_signals` rows + Realtime INSERT + a drain on join | Durable, ordered by `id`, and re-read after any interruption. |
+| Call state | `calls.state`, server transitions | One authority. Clients render it and request transitions. |
+| Presence | existing `initPresence` (unchanged) | Already scoped and working; not rebuilt. |
+| Album changes | `postgres_changes` on `albums`/`album_items` | Lets an expiring album and its removal reach an open screen. |
+
+Deliberately **not** used: Supabase broadcast for anything authoritative. It is
+unauthenticated and fire-and-forget, and both properties caused real failures.
+
+---
+
+## B. Root cause per problem
+
+| # | Reported symptom | Root cause | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | No toast or badge for a message in another conversation | The only subscription was `subscribeToConversationMessages(activeRoomId)` inside an effect keyed `[activeRoomId, supabaseUserId]` | old `App.tsx:1310` |
+| 2 | Badge never appears | `unreadCount={0}` hardcoded; no unread model existed anywhere | old `App.tsx:2067` |
+| 3 | Toast could not be tapped, named no sender, vanished on navigation | A single `notificationToast: string` rendered only while `App` was mounted | old `App.tsx:475/809/2046` |
+| 4 | No notification when the app is closed | No service worker, no manifest, no Push API call | `public/` contained 4 images |
+| 5 | Calls did not ring | Call-request sent over broadcast on a throwaway channel; dropped if the callee was not joined; nothing persisted to retry | old `webrtcService.ts` `startCall` |
+| 6 | Call "connected" but silent | `pc.ontrack → setState('connected')` — a delivered track is not a settled connection | old `setupPeerConnection` |
+| 7 | Call died on a brief network blip | `onconnectionstatechange`: `'disconnected' → failed` with no grace period | old `setupPeerConnection` |
+| 8 | Call stuck "connected" after the peer vanished | No heartbeat and no server sweep; teardown was local only | old `cleanup()` |
+| 9 | Call failed behind restrictive NATs | `getIceServers()` returned STUN only unless `VITE_TURN_*` was set | old `getIceServers` |
+| 10 | TURN credential exposed | Static credential read from `VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL`, inlined into the bundle | old `getIceServers` |
+| 11 | Any third party could signal into a call | Broadcast channels carry no authorisation | old `sendDirectSignal` |
+| 12 | Expired messages came back | `expires_at` written but no read path filtered it | old `loadConversationMessages` |
+| 13 | Message TTL shown for a length never applied | `ephemeralTtlSeconds: targetRoom.ephemeralTtlSeconds` — the client overwrote the row's real lifetime | old `applyRow` |
+| 14 | Disappearing-message setting reverted on reopen | `handleUpdateRoomTtl` only called `setRooms`; nothing was persisted | old `App.tsx` |
+| 15 | Duplicate messages after a retry | No idempotency key | old `persistConversationMessage` |
+| 16 | Expired content removed without a refresh | Subscription listened to INSERT only | old `subscribeToConversationMessages` |
+| 17 | Channels leaked and duplicated on navigation | Channel created per room per mount, removed by hand; React StrictMode double-mounted every effect | old effect + `supabase.channel()` per room |
+| 18 | Messaging stopped after backgrounding | No visibility handling; a suspended iOS socket looks alive but delivers nothing | no `visibilitychange` listener existed |
+
+---
+
