+repository; it does not read the live project. It cannot confirm that the live
+permissive policies match the ones it assumes, so it cannot certify that a
+policy on the live `messages` table is correct — only that the policies in this
+repository behave as specified given a reasonable base. That gap is what the
+preflight exists to close, and closing it requires the operator.
