+# Attic — preserved, not wired in, not typechecked
+
+Six components and one hook that were built on a divergent branch of this
+codebase and do not belong to the application as it stands today.
+
+| File | Why it is here |
+|---|---|
+| `MemberPhotoRail.tsx` | Loads **another member's** photos. The current `profilePhotoService` reads only the signed-in user's `profile_photos`, so the data source this component needs does not exist. |
+| `PhotoViewer.tsx` | Reached only from `MemberPhotoRail`. |
+| `ProfileAlbum.tsx` | Reached only from `MemberPhotoRail`. |
+| `ProfilePhoto.tsx` | Reached only from the two above. |
+| `useSignedPhotoUrl.ts` | Used only by `ProfilePhoto`. |
+| `EditProfileSheet.tsx` | Edits fields (`age`) that `UserProfile` no longer carries, and does not match how the current profile editing works. |
+
+## What "attic" means here
+
+- **Nothing was deleted.** Every file is intact, and each one is also in the git
+  history, so nothing is lost either way.
+- **Nothing in the app imports these.** Verified: no file outside this directory
+  references any of them, so removing them from the compile would not change the
+  bundle even if they compiled.
+- **They are excluded from `tsc`** (see `tsconfig.json`). They were written
+  against an earlier version of `types.ts` and `profilePhotoService.ts` and would
+  need real work — a peer-photo data source that does not exist yet — to become
+  correct. Excluding them keeps `npm run typecheck` meaningful for the
+  application instead of permanently red because of dead code.
+- **The build ignores them.** Vite only bundles what `main.tsx` reaches, so none
+  of this ships.
+
+## Reviving one
+
+Move it back into `src/components/` (or `src/hooks/`), fix its imports, give it a
+real data source, and delete this note's row for it. Do not wire one in without
+the data source — `MemberPhotoRail` would silently render nothing.
