@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# GAYZE — Supabase backend
+
+The client talks to Supabase through `src/services/supabaseService.ts`,
+`src/services/profilePhotoService.ts` and `src/services/supabaseClient.ts`. Only the
+publishable key ever reaches the browser; there is no service-role key in the frontend
+environment, by design.
+
+## Applying the schema
+
+There was no migration tracked in this repository before, so the contract the client
+depends on lives in [`docs/BACKEND_REQUIREMENTS.md`](../docs/BACKEND_REQUIREMENTS.md) and
+the migrations directory is where new backend work goes.
+
+| Migration | What it adds |
+| --- | --- |
+| `20260928120000_profile_photos.sql` | `profiles.avatar_path`, `profiles.interests`, the `profile_photos` table + RLS, the private `profile-photos` storage bucket + object policies, and the `mark_primary_profile_photo` / `reorder_profile_photos` RPCs. |
+
+Apply it in the Supabase SQL editor, or with the CLI:
+
+```bash
+supabase link --project-ref <your-project-ref>
+supabase db push
+```
+
+Every statement is idempotent, so running it against a database that is already
+partially migrated is safe.
+
+## What the client does when the backend is not migrated
+
+It reports it. There is no fallback image, no placeholder score and no seeded photo:
+
+* the album renders **“Photo library not available yet”** rather than an empty frame or
+  a stand-in picture,
+* the trust panel renders **“no history yet”** and **“Not verified”** rather than a
+  default score,
+* uploads fail with the reason, and the settings say which object is missing.
+
+## Storage layout and privacy
+
+```
+profile-photos/            (private bucket, 5 MB limit, JPEG/PNG/WebP)
+  └── {user_id}/
+        └── {photo_id}.{ext}
+```
+
+* The bucket is **private**. Objects are never public and are never linked directly.
+  The browser receives a short-lived signed URL (`createSignedUrl`, 1 hour) and the
+  service caches it in memory for its lifetime — nothing is written to `localStorage`.
+* Writes are owner-only, enforced twice: by the Storage policy
+  (`(storage.foldername(name))[1] = auth.uid()::text`) and by a table constraint that
+  pins `storage_path` to `{user_id}/{photo_id}.{ext}`.
+* Reads obey `public.gayze_can_view_profile_media(owner)`: you can read your own media,
+  anyone can read a member's media while that member is genuinely live on the map (an
+  unexpired, unpaused intent row), and people who already share a conversation with them
+  keep access afterwards so photos do not vanish mid-conversation.
+* `profiles.avatar_path` is maintained by trigger from `profile_photos`. Clients never
+  write it. `discover_right_now` already returns it as `avatar_path`, which is how a
+  member's face reaches Right Now and Discover.
+
+## Security invariants
+
+* A member can never overwrite or delete another member's media, by policy and by path
+  shape.
+* Trust data (`reliability_score`, `verified_peers_count`, `safety_verified`) is
+  backend-owned. The client never sends these values; `saveSupabaseProfileEdits` writes
+  only display name, handle, bio, age, interests and privacy setting.
+* Conversation keys, identity keys and device fingerprints are unrelated to this
+  bucket and are never stored in it.
