+/**
+ * Phase 2 — migration integrity, executed against real PostgreSQL.
+ *
+ * These are the checks the brief asks for, turned into assertions rather than
+ * a claim in a report. Three of them exist because the previous phase's
+ * migrations had exactly these defects and nothing caught them:
+ *
+ *   * functions revoked from PUBLIC and granted to nobody, so the server-side
+ *     caller (service_role — not a superuser) could not invoke them;
+ *   * new tables created with no grants at all, so every query returned
+ *     "permission denied" before RLS was even consulted;
+ *   * a grant placed above the definition of the function it named, which is a
+ *     hard error at apply time.
